      "automation_source": "clawsweeper",
      "repair_reason": "- [P1] Needs human security-boundary review because the fix direction changes command identity; an automated repair would mostly remove or re-scope the proposed behavior rather than finish it.; Needs attention: The diff changes exec approval parsing and has concrete security-boundary concerns around misclassifying wrapper operands as executables.; Review finding: [P1] Keep flock separators before the lock target — s... (sha=fe5e06d5556885a33e96dc3856179549bbb57e7d)",
      "review_summary": "The PR changes dispatch wrapper resolution so `flock` skips a `--` token after the lock target and BSD-style `script` treats a consumed `--` as making the remaining tokens the command.\n\nPR surface: Source +5. Total +5 across 1 file.\n\nReproducibility: yes. for the PR-introduced defect: source inspection plus util-linux live behavior and FreeBSD source show the new branches can unwrap operands that are not the executed command. I did not run the PR branch itself.",
      "review_followup": "- [P1] Needs human security-boundary review because the fix direction changes command identity; an automated repair would mostly remove or re-scope the proposed behavior rather than finish it.",
